A||||1||olympic||Fixing nicks in a polished aluminum wheel||||1||
Z||000000||olympic||09-03-2000||11:15 PM||||  I bought a used set of wheels that have a bright polished finish and there are a few small nicks and scratches on them.  I was wondering if I could fix the damage with the polishing procedure detailed in a few other threads.  Namely :wet sanding a small area around the damage with 220, 400, 600 grit and then buffing with stainless, tripoli and white rouge.   Could I sand by hand or would I need an orbital sander?  Any input here would be appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-04-2000||03:15 PM||||You could try that. Good luck. blending that into a polished finish won't be fun. (Depends just how polished they are.) <P>How big are the nicks..... You'll likely need to do it by hand for small stuff. Most power tools won't have fine enough control.||||reg||1
